    <h2>1. What Will You Build Today?</h2>
    <p>Congratulations! You have learned HTML from Lesson 1 to Lesson 9. Now it is time to <b>use everything together</b> and build your first complete website.</p>
    <p>Today you will build a <b>Personal Portfolio Website</b> - a website about yourself. This is the same website that real developers make to show their work and get jobs.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Your Project Will Have:</b> Header + Nav + About + Skills (List) + Marks (Table) + Contact (Form) + Footer. All in one page!</div>
    <h2>2. What You Learned - Quick Revision</h2>
    <div class="checklist">
      ✅ Lesson 1 - What is HTML?<br>
      ✅ Lesson 2 - Headings & Paragraphs<br>
      ✅ Lesson 3 - Text Formatting - b, i, u, strong<br>
      ✅ Lesson 4 - Links & Images - a, img<br>
      ✅ Lesson 5 - Lists - ul, ol, li<br>
      ✅ Lesson 6 - Tables - table, tr, td, th<br>
      ✅ Lesson 7 - Forms - form, input, label, button<br>
      ✅ Lesson 8 - Div & Span - div, span, class, id<br>
      ✅ Lesson 9 - Semantic HTML - header, nav, main, section, footer
    </div>
    <h2>3. Project Plan - 6 Sections</h2>
    <table>
