    <h2>6. 5 Rules For A Good Project</h2>
    <p><b>1. Use Semantic Tags:</b> Use header, nav, main, section, footer - not only div.<br><b>2. Use Headings Correctly:</b> Only one h1 per page. Then h2, then h3.<br><b>3. Use alt in Images:</b> Always write alt="My Photo" in img tag.<br><b>4. Close All Tags:</b> Every opening tag must have a closing tag.<br><b>5. Change The Content:</b> Do not copy Ali's name. Put your own name, your own skills, your own marks.</p>
    <h2>7. Homework - Build Your Own Project in 15 Minutes</h2>
    <p>Go to Playground and build your own portfolio:</p>
    <p>1. Change name to <b>your name</b><br>2. Change skills to <b>your 3 skills</b><br>3. Change marks table to <b>your marks</b><br>4. Add your <b>favourite foods list</b> - ul<br>5. Add your <b>daily routine</b> - ol<br>6. Take a screenshot and share it with your friend</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> HTML Project = Lesson 1 to 9 Together | header + nav + main + section + table + form + footer = Full Website | You are now ready for CSS - Lesson 11 will make this same website beautiful!</div>
